    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the clear headliner, boasting an elite 81.88 score. His matchup against Grant Holmes is ideal, with an xERA of 4.75 providing a high-ceiling environment that is further bolstered by park factors and a strong platoon advantage, making him a cornerstone for production across all five categories. Following him, **Drake Baldwin** (68.48) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) lead our efforts to secure stolen bases, with both benefiting from projected leadoff spots and favorable pitcher-delivery metrics that favor high-aggression baserunning. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.81) remains a primary anchor, successfully navigating the SP skill deficit against Patrick Sandoval by leveraging his consistent recency profile and favorable order placement.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal gap between our final utility spots and the bench. **Miguel Vargas** was the odd man out with a score of 60.53; while he shows strong metrics against Spencer Arrighetti, including a favorable xwOBA and stolen base potential due to the pitcher's slow delivery, the optimizer opted for the higher-upside profiles of **Heliot Ramos** (64.64) and **Jacob Wilson** (62.24). **Heliot Ramos** particularly stands out for his ability to capitalize on wind-aided conditions and a matchup against Grayson Rodriguez, despite the slight suppression caused by an elite opposing catcher's pop time. \n\nManagement notes that nearly all starting positions remain dependent on \"Lineup Pending\" status, which introduces volatility to our projected order advantages. While the scores for **Liam Hicks** (56.65), **Kyle Tucker** (57.25), and **Andy Pages** (54.25) are serviceable, they are currently the most vulnerable to negative variance should their confirmed batting positions shift downward. We are monitoring these lineups closely; if **Kyle Tucker** or **Andy Pages** are shifted out of premium spots against Sean Manaea, their utility becomes strictly marginal, and we may look to hedge if the late-game environment dictates a shift toward pure stolen base volume.",
